  "final_answer": "All four deliverables are written to `/app` and verified consistent.\n\n**`collateral_audit.csv`** \u2014 60 in-scope items (the 6 `standalone_graphic`/`vehicle_wrap` items are excluded per \u00a71), `item_id,finding` only.\n\n**`zone_summary.csv`** \u2014 8 zones, `zone_id,item_count,pulled_count,standing_area_sqft,aggregate_allowance_sqft,allowance`.\n\n**`collateral_memo.md`** \u2014 memo for the safety office covering the review date, out-of-scope items, every flagged item with its deciding record, the equality-cleared items, zones over allowance, and the heightened-inspection effect.\n\n**`results.json`** \u2014 the eleven \u00a77 figures:\n- `collateral_count` 60, `zone_count` 8\n- `permit_missing_count` 20, `egress_obstructed_count` 8, `oversize_count` 13\n- `compliant_count` 21, `flagged_count` 39, `finding_total` 41\n- `out_of_scope_count` 6, `pulled_item_count` 20, `zones_over_allowance` 3\n\nKey outcomes: **heightened inspection is in force** (3 zones \u2014 ZN-03, ZN-07, ZN-08 \u2014 over allowance, meeting the \u00a76 threshold), which tightened the size cap by 1 sq ft in those zones and newly raised `OVERSIZE_COLLATERAL` on COL-15, COL-16, COL-42, COL-48 and COL-50. The two supersession traps (COL-10/COL-31 named a covering permit but the re-issued governing row PMT-1006 is narrower; COL-35's PMT-1007 was superseded by the lapsed PMT-1008) all return `PERMIT_NUMBER_MISSING` and are pulled.",
